When building an app, protecting user data requires security at **every layer**: mobile app, backend, database, authentication, storage, and infrastructure. Here is a complete checklist you can follow (especially for a Flutter + Supabase/Laravel app).

# 1. Authentication Security

✅ **Use secure authentication**

* Use OAuth (Google, Apple, Microsoft) where possible
* Use secure email/password authentication
* Never store passwords yourself
* Store only hashed passwords (bcrypt/Argon2)

For Supabase:

* Enable Supabase Auth
* Use email verification
* Enable MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication)

Protect against:

* Brute-force attacks
* Account takeover
* Credential stuffing

---

# 2. Password Security

Never store:

❌ Plain passwords
❌ Passwords in databases
❌ Passwords in logs

Use:

✅ Strong password rules:

* Minimum 8–12 characters
* Uppercase + lowercase
* Numbers
* Symbols

Example:

```
OdiApp@2026Secure
```

Use:

* Argon2id
* bcrypt

---

# 3. Database Security

For Supabase/PostgreSQL:

## Enable Row Level Security (RLS)

This is one of the most important protections.

Example:

Users should only see their own profile:

```sql
CREATE POLICY "Users can view own profile"
ON profiles
FOR SELECT
USING (auth.uid() = id);
```

Without RLS:

❌ User A could access User B's data.

With RLS:

✅ Users only access allowed data.

---

# 4. API Security

Protect your backend APIs.

Use:

✅ Authentication tokens
✅ JWT validation
✅ Rate limiting
✅ Request validation
✅ API keys restrictions

Example:

Bad:

```
GET /users/123
```

Anyone can access.

Better:

```
GET /users/123
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
```

---

# 5. Never Expose Secret Keys

Never put these inside Flutter:

❌ Database password
❌ Supabase service_role key
❌ AWS secret keys
❌ Payment secret keys

Flutter apps can be reverse engineered.

Safe:

```
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
```

Unsafe:

```
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
```

Keep secrets on:

* Backend server
* Environment variables

Example:

```
.env

DATABASE_PASSWORD=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
```

---

# 6. Secure Data Storage on Mobile

Do not store sensitive data using:

❌ SharedPreferences
❌ Plain text files
❌ Local databases without encryption

Use:

Flutter:

✅ flutter_secure_storage

Stores:

* Tokens
* Refresh tokens
* Encryption keys

---

# 7. Encryption

## Data in transit

Always use:

✅ HTTPS
✅ TLS 1.2+

Never:

```
http://api.example.com
```

Use:

```
https://api.example.com
```

---

## Data at rest

Encrypt sensitive data:

Examples:

* Phone numbers
* Addresses
* Medical records
* Payment information

Use:

* AES-256 encryption

---

# 8. User Privacy Protection

Only collect what you need.

Bad:

Collect:

* Full address
* Birthday
* Contacts
* Location

when unnecessary.

Good:

Only collect:

* Name
* Email
* Required information

Follow:

* GDPR
* Data Protection Act
* Privacy policies

---

# 9. Secure File Uploads

For profile pictures, documents, videos:

Protect against:

* Malware uploads
* Fake file types
* Huge files

Implement:

✅ File size limits

Example:

```
Maximum image size: 5MB
Maximum video: 100MB
```

Check:

* File extension
* MIME type

Store files securely:

* Supabase Storage
* Cloudinary
* AWS S3

---

# 10. Session Security

Protect login sessions:

Use:

✅ Short-lived access tokens

Example:

```
Access token:
15 minutes

Refresh token:
30 days
```

Implement:

* Logout everywhere
* Token rotation
* Session expiry

---

# 11. Input Validation

Never trust user input.

Protect against:

* SQL injection
* XSS
* Code injection

Example:

Bad:

```sql
SELECT * FROM users WHERE email='$email'
```

Safe:

Use prepared statements:

```sql
SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=?
```

---

# 12. Prevent SQL Injection

Use:

✅ ORM

Examples:

Laravel:

```php
User::where('email',$email)->first();
```

Not:

```php
DB::raw($input)
```

---

# 13. Prevent XSS Attacks

When displaying user content:

Escape:

```html
<script>alert("hack")</script>
```

should display as text, not execute.

---

# 14. Secure Payments

If your app handles payments:

Never store:

❌ Card numbers
❌ CVV
❌ Bank details

Use:

* Stripe
* PayPal
* Flutterwave

They handle PCI compliance.

---

# 15. Logging Security

Never log:

❌ Passwords
❌ Tokens
❌ Personal information

Bad:

```
User login:
email=test@gmail.com
password=123456
```

Good:

```
User login successful
User ID: 93848
```

---

# 16. Admin Dashboard Security

Protect admin panels:

Use:

✅ Role-based access control (RBAC)

Example:

Roles:

```
Admin
Manager
Customer
Seller
Support
```

Permissions:

```
Admin:
Delete users

Customer:
View own account
```

---

# 17. Two-Factor Authentication

Add:

* Authenticator apps
* SMS verification
* Email codes

Examples:

* Google Authenticator
* Authy

---

# 18. Device Security

For mobile apps:

Add:

* Root detection
* Jailbreak detection
* App integrity checks

---

# 19. App Code Protection

Flutter:

Enable:

```
flutter build apk --obfuscate --split-debug-info
```

This makes reverse engineering harder.

---

# 20. Dependency Security

Keep packages updated.

Check:

Flutter:

```
flutter pub outdated
```

Node:

```
npm audit
```

Laravel:

```
composer audit
```

---

# 21. Backup & Recovery

Have:

✅ Database backups
✅ Disaster recovery plan
✅ Restore testing

For Supabase:

* Enable backups
* Test restoration

---

# 22. Monitoring

Monitor:

* Failed logins
* Suspicious activity
* API abuse
* Database changes

Tools:

* Sentry
* Firebase Crashlytics
* Supabase Logs

---

# 23. Security Testing

Before launch:

Test:

✅ Authentication
✅ Permissions
✅ APIs
✅ Database rules
✅ File uploads

Tools:

* OWASP ZAP
* Burp Suite
* SonarQube

---

# 24. Secure Development Practices

Use:

✅ Git branches
✅ Code reviews
✅ Environment variables
✅ Secrets management

Never upload:

```
.env
google-services.json
service_role keys
```

to GitHub.

---

# 25. Follow OWASP Mobile Security Rules

The main threats:

1. Improper authentication
2. Insecure storage
3. Insecure communication
4. Code tampering
5. Poor cryptography
6. Privacy leaks
7. Poor authorization

---

## For your Flutter + Supabase + Laravel app, the minimum security setup should be:

✅ Supabase Auth
✅ Email verification
✅ MFA
✅ Row Level Security (RLS)
✅ HTTPS only
✅ Secure storage in Flutter
✅ Laravel API authentication
✅ Role permissions
✅ Encrypted sensitive data
✅ Cloudinary/Supabase secure uploads
✅ Rate limiting
✅ Monitoring
✅ Regular backups

That setup is close to what production apps use.
